module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.HigherDirectImageBaseChangeAffine
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ModuleFlatBaseChangeQuasicoherent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.GlobalSectionsPullbackBaseChange
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ModuleBaseChangeMapHorizontal

/-!
# Global sections after flat base change over an affine base are spanned by pullbacks

Let

```
X' --g'--> X
|f'         |f
v           v
Y' --g-->  Y
```

be a cartesian square of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S` of a big fppf site, with `Y` and `Y'`
affine, `g` flat and `f` quasi-compact and quasi-separated, and let `𝓕` be a quasi-coherent
`𝒪_X`-module. Flat base change in degree zero says `Γ(X', (g')^*𝓕) = Γ(Y', 𝒪) ⊗_{Γ(Y, 𝒪)} Γ(X, 𝓕)`;
this file records the consequence that is used downstream: every global section of `(g')^*𝓕` is
a `Γ(X', 𝒪)`-linear combination of pullbacks of global sections of `𝓕`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.globalSectionsPushforwardIsoSite_baseChange_pullbackMap`:
  the degree-zero base change map, read on global sections, carries the pullback of a global
  section of `f_*𝓕` along `g` to the pullback along `g'` of the corresponding global section of
  `𝓕`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_span_range_pullbackSection`:
  **the pullbacks of global sections span**: the `Γ(X', 𝒪)`-submodule of `Γ(X', (g')^*𝓕)` spanned
  by the pullbacks along `g'` of the global sections of `𝓕` is everything.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_span_baseScalars_range_pullbackSection`: the same, with the
  coefficients taken in `Γ(Y', 𝒪)`, acting on `Γ(X', (g')^*𝓕)` through `f'`.

## Implementation notes

The isomorphism is the composite of three existing ones: global sections of an inverse image over
affine bases (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isIso_globalSectionsPullbackBaseChange`), the degree-zero
clause of Stacks 073K, part (1), `g^*f_*𝓕 ≅ f'_*(g')^*𝓕`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isIso_moduleBaseChangeMap_app_of_isFlat`), and Stacks 0732 for `f'`.
That the composite sends `1 ⊗ s` to the pullback of `s` is the mate identity on global sections,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.BaseChangeDiagram.globalSectionsPushforwardIsoSite_square_component`.

The square and the coefficient are taken as separate arguments rather than bundled in a
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.BaseChangeDiagram`: a consumer building the square from a scheme point
then never has to compare the projections of a bundled diagram with the data it was built from,
a comparison the elaborator makes slowly inside the large terms involved.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 073K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/073K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0732](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0732)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

